## 🗄️ Database Design & Schema
The database named `bank_management` contains four major tables: `customers`, `accounts`, `transactions`, and `admins`.

### Schema Details:

| Table | Column Name | Data Type | Key / Constraints | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`customers`** | `customer_id` | INT | Primary Key, Auto Increment | Unique internal identifier for each customer |
| | `name` | VARCHAR(100) | NOT NULL | Customer's full name |
| | `email` | VARCHAR(100) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Customer's unique email address (login identifier) |
| | `phone` | VARCHAR(15) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Customer's unique phone number |
| | `password` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL | Password for customer portal access |
| | `address` | VARCHAR(255) | Nullable | Optional physical address |
| | `created_at` | TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Date/time of record creation |
| **`accounts`** | `account_no` | INT | Primary Key (starts at 1001) | Unique account number |
| | `customer_id` | INT | Foreign Key (→ `customers.customer_id`) | References the owner of the account (ON DELETE CASCADE) |
| | `account_type` | VARCHAR(20) | NOT NULL | Type of account (e.g., SAVINGS, CURRENT) |
| | `balance` | DECIMAL(15,2)| DEFAULT 0.00 | Current account balance |
| | `status` | VARCHAR(20) | DEFAULT 'ACTIVE' | Account state (ACTIVE, CLOSED, etc.) |
| **`transactions`** | `transaction_id`| INT | Primary Key, Auto Increment | Unique transaction identifier |
| | `from_account`| INT | Foreign Key (→ `accounts.account_no`) | Originating account (ON DELETE CASCADE, Nullable for external deposits) |
| | `to_account` | INT | Foreign Key (→ `accounts.account_no`) | Receiving account (ON DELETE CASCADE, Nullable for external withdrawals) |
| | `transaction_type`| VARCHAR(20)| NOT NULL | E.g., DEPOSIT, WITHDRAWAL, TRANSFER |
| | `amount` | DECIMAL(15,2)| NOT NULL | Amount transacted |
| | `transaction_time`| TIMESTAMP | DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP | Date/time of transaction execution |
| | `remarks` | VARCHAR(255) | Nullable | Custom user remarks |
| **`admins`** | `admin_id` | INT | Primary Key, Auto Increment | Unique administrator ID |
| | `username` | VARCHAR(50) | NOT NULL, UNIQUE | Username for admin login |
| | `password` | VARCHAR(255) | NOT NULL | Password for admin login |

*Note: Default admin credentials are username: `admin` / password: `admin123`.*

